%I A400568 #14 Oct 08 2026 18:53:05
%S A400568 1,1,8,52,734,55883
%N A400568 Number of nonisomorphic dimonoids of order n.
%C A400568 A dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A400568   (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A400568   (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z),
%C A400568   (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%H A400568 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00927872.2026.2712633">On dimonoids of small order</a>, Commun. Algebra, 1-15 (2026).
%H A400568 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.17921">On dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.17921 [math.GR], 2026.
%H A400568 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22646150">Lists of All Pairwise Nonisomorphic Dimonoids of Orders up to 5</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400568 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/b41c66cce83a13e008168d06e0b6988d">Python code for computing nonisomorphic dimonoids</a>.
%e A400568 For n = 2, there are exactly 8 pairwise nonisomorphic dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all eight dimonoids are listed below.
%e A400568 Dimonoid #1:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 0
%e A400568   0 0   0 0
%e A400568 Dimonoid #2:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 1
%e A400568   0 0   0 1
%e A400568 Dimonoid #3:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 1   0 1
%e A400568   1 0   1 0
%e A400568 Dimonoid #4:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 0
%e A400568   0 1   0 1
%e A400568 Dimonoid #5:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 0
%e A400568   1 1   0 0
%e A400568 Dimonoid #6:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 0
%e A400568   1 1   1 1
%e A400568 Dimonoid #7:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 0   0 1
%e A400568   1 1   0 1
%e A400568 Dimonoid #8:
%e A400568   -|:   |-:
%e A400568   0 1   0 1
%e A400568   0 1   0 1
%Y A400568 Cf. A027851, A400569, A400570.
%K A400568 nonn,more,new
%O A400568 0,3
